# Pairs with NoKeyLost. The write gate does not refuse a sealed slot, so a
# router still holding an old map writes k2 to a shard that no longer owns it
# and the write is acknowledged without reaching the owner.
MODULE: NoKeyLostFoldLaterWriteIgnoresSeal
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a write through a stale map lands on a shard whose seal should refuse it
PERTURBS: LaterOp

--- FIND
       IN /\ ~Refused(s, k2)
          /\ row' = [x \in Shards |-> [k \in Keys |->
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the seal does not refuse the write.
       IN /\ row' = [x \in Shards |-> [k \in Keys |->
--- END
